============================================================================================================== 
1. PARAMETERS: prior -> posterior (percent, 94% HDI)

z   P(not exactly one other output | composer ignores the rule)
      prior Beta(2,10): median 14.80 mean 16.66 [94% HDI 0.83, 35.45]
      post  (payload deposits 2024-26, 149/451, design effect 4): median 31.39 mean 31.48 [94% HDI 23.80, 39.39]
      alt   (all payload deposits 170/703): median 23.60 mean 23.69 [94% HDI 18.07, 29.63]
      alt   (2023 only 21/252): median 9.33 mean 9.68 [94% HDI 3.75, 15.96]
      alt   (2026 only 41/92): median 34.67 mean 34.95 [94% HDI 20.43, 49.81]
u   share of flags-03 deposits from composers that do not check the rule
      prior lognormal(median 3%, 97th pct 20%): median 2.99 mean 4.95 [94% HDI 0.08, 14.28]
      post  (LR 0.6-1.0 single composer; LR 1.0-1.5 silent failure): median 2.86 mean 4.80 [94% HDI 0.08, 14.04]
s   slip rate of a checking composer: LU(0.02%, 1%), unchanged: median 0.14 mean 0.25 [94% HDI 0.02, 0.79]
g   P(a flags-03 deposit breaks the rule) = u*z + (1-u)*s
      prior LU(0.1%, 5%): median 0.71 mean 1.25 [94% HDI 0.10, 3.95]
      post : median 1.17 mean 1.75 [94% HDI 0.07, 4.69]
v   share of flagged deposits where the signing wallet verifies change as its own
      prior Beta(3,2): median 61.42 mean 59.97 [94% HDI 24.40, 95.13]
      post  Beta(3,4) (0 of 3 signing integrations of the official app, counted as 2 observations): median 42.17 mean 42.84 [94% HDI 11.19, 74.88]
d_c P(payer notices a substituted change output) = v*U(50,90%) + (1-v)*U(5,35%)
      prior U(25%, 90%): median 57.53 mean 57.49 [94% HDI 25.01, 86.10]
      post : median 41.07 mean 41.42 [94% HDI 19.73, 63.49]
d_f P(payer notices a substituted refund field): U(0, 20%) unchanged: median 10.01 mean 10.01 [94% HDI 0.41, 19.20]
e_c honest error, the single other output is not the payer's
      prior LU(0.1%, 3%): median 0.55 mean 0.85 [94% HDI 0.10, 2.45]
      post  (8/533 type mismatches, design effect 4, flat nuisance; importance sampling, ESS 356,155): median 0.52 mean 0.80 [94% HDI 0.10, 2.31]
e_f honest error, the refund field names an address the payer cannot use
      prior LU(0.2%, 5%): median 1.00 mean 1.49 [94% HDI 0.20, 4.13]
      post  central (prior x LU(1, 2.5)): median 1.57 mean 2.44 [94% HDI 0.20, 6.89]
      alt   no shift: median 1.00 mean 1.49 [94% HDI 0.20, 4.13]
      alt   strong carry-over (117/335 x keep U(1,15%) x share U(30,90%) added): median 2.90 mean 3.15 [94% HDI 0.52, 6.10]
w   P(no sender-derived address | rule broken) (first-draft rule only)
      prior U(50%, 95%): median 72.47 mean 72.51 [94% HDI 51.35, 93.59]
      post  (154/170, design effect 4): median 89.33 mean 88.76 [94% HDI 80.06, 96.83]
rho, h: unchanged (rho U(2%,30%), h LU(0.05%,2%)); the survey does not inform them

============================================================================================================== 
2. RESULTS

Earlier pass (priors), reproduced:
   (a) refund reaches the payer | refund due, deposit has change              P(change better) 0.74; advantage median +0.622 pp [-1.813, +4.128], mean +0.882
   (c) per flagged deposit, as computed then (loss g*w*rho)                   P(change better) 0.48; advantage median -0.006 pp [-0.664, +0.672], mean -0.002
       same, corrected: adopted rule builds no release, so w = 1              P(change better) 0.43; advantage median -0.031 pp [-0.809, +0.682], mean -0.058

After the survey, central (e_f raised by a factor 1 to 2.5):
   (a)  refund reaches the payer | refund due, deposit has change             P(change better) 0.81; advantage median +1.074 pp [-2.028, +6.566], mean +1.789
   (a') refund reaches the payer | refund due (includes deposits without change) P(change better) 0.46; advantage median -0.183 pp [-5.077, +6.645], mean +0.057
   (b)  per flagged deposit, adopted rule                                     P(change better) 0.46; advantage median -0.019 pp [-0.954, +1.180], mean +0.009
        per flagged deposit, first-draft rule (parse failure)                 P(change better) 0.11; advantage median -0.833 pp [-4.328, +1.112], mean -1.266
     median loss per flagged deposit: payload 0.298 pp; change (adopted) 0.337 pp; means 0.463 vs 0.454 pp

After the survey, STRONG e_f carry-over:
   (a)  refund reaches the payer | refund due, deposit has change             P(change better) 0.94; advantage median +2.313 pp [-0.679, +6.004], mean +2.504
   (b)  per flagged deposit, adopted rule                                     P(change better) 0.67; advantage median +0.099 pp [-0.667, +1.109], mean +0.122

After the survey, e_f NOT shifted (stays at its prior):
   (a)  refund reaches the payer | refund due, deposit has change             P(change better) 0.73; advantage median +0.556 pp [-1.701, +4.096], mean +0.846
   (a') refund reaches the payer | refund due (includes deposits without change) P(change better) 0.33; advantage median -0.687 pp [-4.665, +3.715], mean -0.884
   (b)  per flagged deposit, adopted rule                                     P(change better) 0.33; advantage median -0.077 pp [-0.910, +0.657], mean -0.140

What moved (a): one-at-a-time, starting from the earlier priors
   d_c only                                                                   P(change better) 0.72; advantage median +0.532 pp [-1.895, +4.023], mean +0.800
   e_c only                                                                   P(change better) 0.75; advantage median +0.654 pp [-1.704, +4.133], mean +0.934
   e_f only                                                                   P(change better) 0.81; advantage median +1.139 pp [-2.067, +6.646], mean +1.823
What moved (b, adopted rule, w = 1): one-at-a-time
   g only                                                                     P(change better) 0.34; advantage median -0.071 pp [-0.937, +0.652], mean -0.135
   e_f only                                                                   P(change better) 0.55; advantage median +0.025 pp [-0.846, +1.140], mean +0.093
   d_c and e_c only                                                           P(change better) 0.41; advantage median -0.034 pp [-0.818, +0.646], mean -0.063

Break-even (adopted rule): change equals payload when g = (cp - cc)/(1 - cc)
   g* : median 1.08 mean 1.80 [94% HDI -1.97, 6.74]
   u* (share of non-checking composers at break-even, 0 if g* < s): median 2.76 mean 5.74 [94% HDI 0.00, 20.05]
   e_f not shifted: g* median 0.56 mean 0.85 [94% HDI -1.74, 4.13]
                           u* median 1.08 mean 2.95 [94% HDI 0.00, 11.02]
   posterior medians: rho=0.1598, h=0.0032, d_f=0.1001, d_c=0.4107, e_f=0.0157, e_c=0.0052, z=0.3139, s=0.0014, u=0.0286, g=0.0117

